// An OPTIONAL-CHAIN result as an operand of a nullable-struct equality. `vl check` returns 0 and
// the emitter refuses with `emitProgram: struct equality over a non-struct operand`
// (`compiler/wasmEmit.vl:11809`). Should print true.
//
// MECHANISM. `o?.f` banks type `S | null`, so the compare classifies as the `nulstruct` niche
// and routes to `emitNulStructEq`. That path resolves each operand's struct row through
// `structIndexOfExpr` (`emit_classify.vl:28840`), whose arms are ObjLit / Paren / IfStmt /
// BinExpr / Call / Ident / Index / Member — and NOT `OptMember`. The `?.` operand falls to the
// `-1` tail, `binEqNulVariantRow` also declines, and the `siFound` guard fires.
//
// EVERY OTHER PRODUCER OF THE SAME TYPE COMPARES FINE, which is what makes this the visitor's
// missing arm and not a rep gap: two locals, two call results, a `(S|null)[]` element, and a
// plain struct-field read `x.f == y.f` all compile and run.
type S = { a: i32 }
type T = { f: S }
function go(o: T | null, q: S | null): boolean { return o?.f == q }
print(go(null, null))
